"""exec-circuit: fixed daily circuits with guaranteed coverage.

At hour 0 of every day the farm's work is enumerated tile by tile from the engine cadence (window crops:
water on window ages, fertilize before the first window watering, harvest+replant at max age; ongoing crops:
water+fertilize on production ages, harvest when yield is present, dig+replant when finished; animals: feed,
care, collect, harvest).  The stops are partitioned into one compact route per unit (farthest-first cheapest
insertion, then local moves), cost = loading + actions + path length (+ return-drop), each within the unit's
step budget.  Units load exactly what their route needs at the shed (feed wheat, fertilizer), seeds for the
day's replants are bought at hour 1, produce is carried and auto-dropped at day end (return-drops only when the
day's produce would overflow the shed).  Idle units help units that are behind.  Stdlib only.
"""
